                <pb facs="0463" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3920: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-22T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1921—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 22—10:14
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>227. Following from Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 21, 5 p.m. Hostilities have commenced between Kwangtung and
                            Kwangsi. It is reported that Wuchow is being attacked Kwangtung troops.
                            Ch’en Ch’iung-ming, commander-in-chief of the Kwangtung forces, is at
                            the front”.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
